{"declarations":[{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Data/URI.html#Std.Http.URI.Path.parseOrRoot\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">URI</span>.<span class=\"name\">Path</span>.<span class=\"name\">parseOrRoot</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">s</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#String\">String</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Std/Http/Data/URI/Basic.html#Std.Http.URI.Path\">Path</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Parses a URI path from the given string. Returns the root path `\"/\"` if parsing fails.\n","docLink":"./Std/Http/Data/URI.html#Std.Http.URI.Path.parseOrRoot","kind":"def","line":168,"name":"Std.Http.URI.Path.parseOrRoot","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Std/Http/Data/URI.lean#L168-L173"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Data/URI.html#Std.Http.URI.Path.parse?\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">URI</span>.<span class=\"name\">Path</span>.<span class=\"name\">parse?</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">s</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#String\">String</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Option\">Option</a> <a href=\"./Std/Http/Data/URI/Basic.html#Std.Http.URI.Path\">Path</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Attempts to parse a URI path from the given string. Returns `none` if the string is not a valid path.\n","docLink":"./Std/Http/Data/URI.html#Std.Http.URI.Path.parse?","kind":"def","line":161,"name":"Std.Http.URI.Path.parse?","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Std/Http/Data/URI.lean#L161-L166"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Data/URI.html#Std.Http.URI.parse!\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">URI</span>.<span class=\"name\">parse!</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">string</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#String\">String</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Std/Http/Data/URI/Basic.html#Std.Http.URI\">URI</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Parses a `URI` from the given string. Panics if parsing fails. Use `parse?` if you need a safe\noption-returning version.\n","docLink":"./Std/Http/Data/URI.html#Std.Http.URI.parse!","kind":"def","line":149,"name":"Std.Http.URI.parse!","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Std/Http/Data/URI.lean#L149-L157"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Data/URI.html#Std.Http.URI.parse?\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">URI</span>.<span class=\"name\">parse?</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">string</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#String\">String</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Option\">Option</a> <a href=\"./Std/Http/Data/URI/Basic.html#Std.Http.URI\">URI</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Attempts to parse a `URI` from the given string.\n","docLink":"./Std/Http/Data/URI.html#Std.Http.URI.parse?","kind":"def","line":142,"name":"Std.Http.URI.parse?","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Std/Http/Data/URI.lean#L142-L147"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Data/URI.html#Std.Http.URI.originTarget\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">URI</span>.<span class=\"name\">originTarget</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">uri</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Http/Data/URI/Basic.html#Std.Http.URI\">URI</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Std/Http/Data/URI/Basic.html#Std.Http.RequestTarget\">RequestTarget</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Returns the origin-form request target corresponding to this URI, dropping the scheme, authority,\nuser-info, and fragment while preserving the query component.\n\nReference: https://httpwg.org/specs/rfc9112.html#section-3.2.1\n","docLink":"./Std/Http/Data/URI.html#Std.Http.URI.originTarget","kind":"def","line":133,"name":"Std.Http.URI.originTarget","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Std/Http/Data/URI.lean#L133-L140"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Data/URI.html#Std.Http.URI.host?\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">URI</span>.<span class=\"name\">host?</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">uri</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Http/Data/URI/Basic.html#Std.Http.URI\">URI</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Option\">Option</a> <a href=\"./Std/Http/Data/URI/Basic.html#Std.Http.URI.Host\">Host</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"The host this URI addresses, or `none` when the URI carries no authority.\n\nA URI without an authority cannot identify an origin to connect to, so callers that need to\ndispatch a request should treat `none` as malformed input rather than substituting a default host.\n","docLink":"./Std/Http/Data/URI.html#Std.Http.URI.host?","kind":"def","line":124,"name":"Std.Http.URI.host?","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Std/Http/Data/URI.lean#L124-L131"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Data/URI.html#Std.Http.URI.port\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">URI</span>.<span class=\"name\">port</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">uri</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Http/Data/URI/Basic.html#Std.Http.URI\">URI</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#UInt16\">UInt16</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Extracts the numeric port this URI addresses. When the authority omits the port (or parses as empty)\nthe scheme's default port is returned (`80` for `http`, `443` for `https`).\n","docLink":"./Std/Http/Data/URI.html#Std.Http.URI.port","kind":"def","line":112,"name":"Std.Http.URI.port","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Std/Http/Data/URI.lean#L112-L122"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Data/URI.html#Std.Http.URIReference.parse!\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">URIReference</span>.<span class=\"name\">parse!</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">string</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#String\">String</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Std/Http/Data/URI/Basic.html#Std.Http.URIReference\">URIReference</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Parses a `URIReference` from the given string. Panics if parsing fails. Use `parse?` if you need\na safe option-returning version.\n","docLink":"./Std/Http/Data/URI.html#Std.Http.URIReference.parse!","kind":"def","line":98,"name":"Std.Http.URIReference.parse!","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Std/Http/Data/URI.lean#L98-L106"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Data/URI.html#Std.Http.URIReference.parse?\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">URIReference</span>.<span class=\"name\">parse?</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">string</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#String\">String</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Option\">Option</a> <a href=\"./Std/Http/Data/URI/Basic.html#Std.Http.URIReference\">URIReference</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Attempts to parse a `URIReference` from the given string.\n\nAccepts both complete URIs (with scheme) and relative references (without scheme), per RFC 3986\n§4.1. Relative references include protocol-relative (`//host/path`), absolute-path (`/path`),\npath-noscheme (`../other`, `foo/bar`), query-only (`?q=1`), fragment-only (`#sec`), and empty.\n","docLink":"./Std/Http/Data/URI.html#Std.Http.URIReference.parse?","kind":"def","line":85,"name":"Std.Http.URIReference.parse?","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Std/Http/Data/URI.lean#L85-L96"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Data/URI.html#Std.Http.RequestTarget.setQueryParam\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">RequestTarget</span>.<span class=\"name\">setQueryParam</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">target</span> : <a href=\"./Std/Http/Data/URI/Basic.html#Std.Http.RequestTarget\">RequestTarget</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">key </span><span class=\"fn\">value</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#String\">String</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Std/Http/Data/URI/Basic.html#Std.Http.RequestTarget\">RequestTarget</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Inserts or appends a query parameter on this target, preserving its form. Origin-form and absolute-form\ntargets gain the parameter on their existing query; authority-form and asterisk-form targets are\nreturned unchanged because they do not carry a query.\n","docLink":"./Std/Http/Data/URI.html#Std.Http.RequestTarget.setQueryParam","kind":"def","line":68,"name":"Std.Http.RequestTarget.setQueryParam","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Std/Http/Data/URI.lean#L68-L79"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Data/URI.html#Std.Http.RequestTarget.pathOrRoot\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">RequestTarget</span>.<span class=\"name\">pathOrRoot</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Std/Http/Data/URI/Basic.html#Std.Http.RequestTarget\">RequestTarget</a> → <a href=\"./Std/Http/Data/URI/Basic.html#Std.Http.URI.Path\">URI.Path</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Returns the path component of the request target, defaulting to the root path `/` when the target\ncarries no path (asterisk-form or authority-form). Unlike `RequestTarget.path`, the fallback is the\nabsolute root rather than an empty relative path — used by clients that need a well-formed absolute path\nfor cookie matching or logging.\n","docLink":"./Std/Http/Data/URI.html#Std.Http.RequestTarget.pathOrRoot","kind":"def","line":57,"name":"Std.Http.RequestTarget.pathOrRoot","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Std/Http/Data/URI.lean#L57-L66"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Data/URI.html#Std.Http.RequestTarget.originForm!\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">RequestTarget</span>.<span class=\"name\">originForm!</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">path</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#String\">String</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Std/Http/Data/URI/Basic.html#Std.Http.RequestTarget\">RequestTarget</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Creates an origin-form request target from a path string. The path should start with '/' (e.g.,\n\"/api/users\" or \"/search?q=test\"). Panics if the string is not a valid origin-form request target.\n","docLink":"./Std/Http/Data/URI.html#Std.Http.RequestTarget.originForm!","kind":"def","line":47,"name":"Std.Http.RequestTarget.originForm!","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Std/Http/Data/URI.lean#L47-L55"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Data/URI.html#Std.Http.RequestTarget.parse!\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">RequestTarget</span>.<span class=\"name\">parse!</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">string</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#String\">String</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><a href=\"./Std/Http/Data/URI/Basic.html#Std.Http.RequestTarget\">RequestTarget</a></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Parses a `RequestTarget` from the given string. Panics if parsing fails. Use `parse?`\nif you need a safe option-returning version.\n","docLink":"./Std/Http/Data/URI.html#Std.Http.RequestTarget.parse!","kind":"def","line":37,"name":"Std.Http.RequestTarget.parse!","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Std/Http/Data/URI.lean#L37-L45"}},{"header":"<div class=\"decl_header\"><span class=\"decl_kind\">def</span>\n<span class=\"decl_name\"><a class=\"break_within\" href=\"./Std/Http/Data/URI.html#Std.Http.RequestTarget.parse?\"><span class=\"name\">Std</span>.<span class=\"name\">Http</span>.<span class=\"name\">RequestTarget</span>.<span class=\"name\">parse?</span></a></span><span class=\"decl_args\">\n<span class=\"fn\">(<span class=\"fn\">string</span> : <a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#String\">String</a>)</span></span>\n<span class=\"decl_args\"> :</span><div class=\"decl_type\"><span class=\"fn\"><a href=\"./Init/Prelude.html#Option\">Option</a> <a href=\"./Std/Http/Data/URI/Basic.html#Std.Http.RequestTarget\">RequestTarget</a></span></div></div>","info":{"doc":"Attempts to parse a `RequestTarget` from the given string.\n","docLink":"./Std/Http/Data/URI.html#Std.Http.RequestTarget.parse?","kind":"def","line":30,"name":"Std.Http.RequestTarget.parse?","sourceLink":"https://github.com/leanprover/lean4/blob/6a10ac8c22beadecabdbb0919c2b50214762f91d/src/Std/Http/Data/URI.lean#L30-L35"}}],"imports":["Std.Http.Data.URI.Basic","Std.Http.Data.URI.Parser"],"instances":[],"name":"Std.Http.Data.URI"}